course: dictionary
lesson: 14754
title: A word about the future
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A prophecy is a statement that something will happen in the future. It is often made by someone people believe has special knowledge. «The old woman's prophecy said the river would freeze before winter.» The clues are "will happen" and "the future", so a prophecy is a message about what is still to come.
explain: Check the clues in the sentence. If a prophecy «came true», then the thing it said would happen really did happen. Try your meaning in the sentence: "The statement about the future came true" still makes sense, so you have the right idea.
explain: Prophecy is also a word used in religion and stories. In the Bible, a prophecy is a message that Christians and Jews believe comes from God, given through a prophet. In a story, a prophecy often drives the plot, because the hero must act on what it says. In science we make predictions with evidence, not prophecies.
fact: A prophecy is a statement that something will happen in the future.
fact: «Prophecy» is a noun. Its plural is prophecies.
fact: «A prophecy came true» means that what was said about the future did happen.
fact: In the Bible, a prophecy is a message that Christians and Jews believe comes from God, given through a prophet.
fact: A «self-fulfilling prophecy» is a belief that makes itself come true, because people act on it.
exercise: «The old woman's prophecy said the king would fall.» What is a prophecy? | A type of castle wall | A picture of an old woman | *A statement about what will happen in the future | A quiet kind of whisper
exercise: In the story, the prophecy said a hero would save the land. What does «the prophecy came true» mean? | The story was never written down | The land was painted blue | *The hero saved the land, as the statement had said | The hero forgot about the land
exercise: Scientists do not make prophecies. They make ___ based on evidence. | Wishes | Ghosts | *Predictions | Dreams
test: Mia reads: «The wise woman's prophecy said the drought would end in spring.» What is a prophecy here? | A list of spring flowers | A kind of weather map | Ghosts | *A statement that says what will happen in the future
test: What does «a self-fulfilling prophecy» mean? | A prophecy that is always wrong | *A prophecy that makes itself come true, because people act on it | A prophecy written in gold ink | A prophecy about fish
exam: Which sentence uses prophecy correctly? | «The prophecy of the dog was very loud and red.» | «She prophecy the rain in her bedroom.» | «The prophecy was a cold, wet sandwich.» | *«The prophecy said the bridge would collapse, and it did.»
